  "script": "Deep within cold clouds of gas, new stars slowly awaken to light up the universe. Gravitational forces cause these vast molecular regions to collapse inward and gather substantial mass over time. As materials draw tightly together, the center heats up and forms a dense rotating protostellar core. Surrounding debris flattens into a swirling disk where future planets can slowly accumulate from debris. Extreme core temperatures eventually trigger nuclear fusion reactions that power the newly born star. Stellar nucleosynthesis inside the burning core forges heavier chemical elements from simpler hydrogen atoms. Eventually, mature stellar systems stabilize and maintain a steady balance between gravity and internal pressure. When aging stars finally scatter their enriched materials outward, they seed future stellar generations across space.",
